8: tool-responseObservation:
Here is the final answer from your managed agent 'retriever_agent':
### 1. Task outcome (short version):
I retrieved and extracted all occurrences in the provided Prospectus (Link Mobility Group Holding ASA - Prospectus) and Annual Report 2020 that mention adjusted EBITDA, EBITDA, non‑GAAP/alternative performance measures (APMs), reconciliation tables, restatements, and subsequent events. Key findings (short):
- Prospectus (excerpts provided): defines EBITDA and Adjusted EBITDA, states APMs are unaudited/non‑IFRS, and provides reconciliation tables with period-by-period amounts for Revenue, Direct Cost, Gross Profit, EBITDA and Adjusted EBITDA for periods: Six months ended 30 June 2020, Six months ended 30 June 2019, Year ended 31 December 2019, Year ended 31 December 2018, Year ended 31 December 2017; also LTM Adjusted EBITDA for LTM ended 30 June 2020. Adjustments shown: share option program cost, M&A activities costs, restructuring cost and other (with explanatory footnotes). Figures are explicitly labelled not audited for APMs in Prospectus text.
- Annual Report 2020 (excerpts provided): contains comprehensive APM section, definitions of EBITDA and Adjusted EBITDA consistent with Prospectus, segment breakdowns including adjusted EBITDA per segment (2020 and 2019), Group-level reconciliation of Adjusted EBITDA to profit before tax and another reconciliation table showing Operating profit, Depreciation & amortisation, EBITDA, and adjustments to reach Adjusted EBITDA for 2020 and 2019. It also includes Events after reporting date (acquisitions in 2021) and confirms APMs prepared under IFRS and that APMs are provided to enhance performance understanding. The Annual Report numbers appear to be presented in NOK and appear to be audited financial statements (but APM lines are non‑IFRS and the APMs themselves are not labeled as audited — the underlying statutory financials would be audited; the prospectus explicitly said APMs are not audited).

Summary of exact adjusted EBITDA values and key points (short):
- Prospectus table (All amounts in NOK million):
  - Adjusted EBITDA: Six months ended 30 June 2020: 182.6; Six months ended 30 June 2019: 134.2; Year ended 31 Dec 2019: 307.5 (note one excerpt shows 307.5 and another 307.941/307.549 variations — see detailed below); Year ended 31 Dec 2018: 212.0 (or 212.4 in reconciliation); Year ended 31 Dec 2017: 140.0; LTM Adjusted EBITDA (LTM ended 30 June 2020): 356.1.
- Annual Report 2020 (all amounts NOK, in thousands in full statements, but excerpts show amounts as NOK thousands or rounded):
  - Adjusted EBITDA by segment totals to Group: Total Adjusted EBITDA 2020: 390,842 (thousand NOK) and 2019: 307,941 (thousand NOK) in one excerpt; another excerpt shows 390,841 and 307,549 (minor rounding/format differences). The Prospectus six‑month figures are partial period (YTD vs six months) differences. Note: Annual report converts to full-year Group Adjusted EBITDA: 390,841 (2020) vs 307,549/307,941 (2019) — reconcile carefully.

### 2. Task outcome (extremely detailed version):
I reproduce the comprehensive extracted passages and reconciliation tables from the provided excerpts so you can compare period-by-period. I include definitions, reconciliation line items, footnotes, statements about audit status, publication dates when available in excerpts, currency, and any subsequent events or restatements noted in excerpts.

A. Prospectus (Link Mobility Group Holding ASA - Prospectus) — extracted relevant text and tables (verbatim from provided excerpts):
- Non‑IFRS financial measures (excerpt_0):
  - “In this Prospectus, the Group presents certain alternative performance measures ("APMs"), including ... EBITDA, Adjusted EBITDA ... The APMs presented herein are not measurements of financial performance or liquidity under IFRS or other generally accepted accounting principles, are not audited and investors should not consider any such measures to be an alternative to ...”
  - Definitions: Churn Rate, Gross Profit, Gross Margin, EBITDA: “operating profit (loss) adding back depreciation and amortisation.” Adjusted EBITDA: “EBITDA adjusted for mergers and acquisitions costs, restructuring costs and costs related to share option program.” Adjusted EBITDA Margin defined as Adjusted EBITDA as a percentage of operating revenues. LTM Adjusted EBITDA defined as Adjusted EBITDA for the last twelve months from the end of the period.
